  "content": {
    "id": "p3-q9-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "If $x=3$ is a solution of the equation $ax^2-2x+5=0$, then find the other solution.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=15$.",
      "worked": "Substitute $x=3$:\n$$\\begin{align*}9a-6+5&=0\\\\9a&=1\\\\a&=\\frac19\\end{align*}$$\nThe equation becomes\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac19x^2-2x+5&=0\\\\x^2-18x+45&=0\\\\(x-3)(x-15)&=0\\\\x&=3\\text{ or }x=15\\end{align*}$$\nThe other solution is $x=15$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 86
  },
